{"verses": [
{"id": "88:6", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "Confitebúntur cæli mirabília tua ... étenim veritátem tuam", "portuguese": "Os céus darão graças pelas vossas maravilhas ... e também pela vossa verdade", "problem": "mirabilia and veritatem are direct objects of confitebuntur (the heavens will confess/praise your wonders); 'dar graças por' turns them into the cause of thanksgiving. 'étenim' is 'and indeed' rather than 'e também'.", "fix": "Os céus celebrarão as vossas maravilhas, Senhor: * e deveras a vossa verdade na assembleia dos santos."}]},
{"id": "88:13", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "tuum brácchium cum poténtia", "portuguese": "vosso é o braço com potência", "problem": "The Latin is a verbless noun phrase ('your arm with might'); supplying 'é' turns it into a predication of ownership ('the arm is yours'), a sense the Latin does not assert.", "fix": "o vosso braço com potência."}]},
{"id": "88:15", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "qui scit jubilatiónem", "portuguese": "que conhece a aclamação", "problem": "jubilatio is jubilation, joyful shouting; 'aclamação' leans toward the Hebrew teru'ah rather than the Latin word.", "fix": "bem-aventurado o povo que conhece o júbilo."}]},
{"id": "88:19", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "Dómini est assúmptio nostra", "portuguese": "do Senhor é o nosso amparo", "problem": "assumptio is 'our taking-up / being taken up' (LXX antilempsis); 'amparo' is defensible but is also used for suscéptor in 88:27, blurring two distinct Latin words.", "fix": "Porque do Senhor é o nosso acolhimento,"}]},
{"id": "88:34", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "non dispérgam ab eo", "portuguese": "não retirarei dele", "problem": "dispergo is 'scatter, dissipate'; 'retirar' loses the Latin image and follows the Hebrew sense.", "fix": "Mas não dissiparei dele a minha misericórdia:"}]},
{"id": "88:36", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "Si David méntiar", "portuguese": "não mentirei a Davi", "problem": "The Latin keeps the elliptical oath formula ('if I lie to David...'); converting it to a plain negative explains rather than translates the Septuagintal idiom.", "fix": "Uma vez jurei pela minha santidade: se eu mentir a Davi! *"}]},
{"id": "88:45", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "Destruxísti eum ab emundatióne", "portuguese": "Destruístes-lhe a purificação", "problem": "The object of destruxisti is 'eum' (him), with 'ab emundatione' as separation (from his cleansing); the translation makes the purification itself the thing destroyed.", "fix": "Destruístes-o, apartando-o da purificação:"}]}
],
"overall": "A faithful, close rendering of the Latin throughout this long psalm, with Septuagintal features (distulisti Christum, commutationem Christi, cornu, non apponet nocere) kept and pointing marks identical to the Latin in every verse. No critical or major faults; the minor points concern a few objects/constructions altered (88:6, 88:13, 88:45), one resolved oath formula (88:36), and a couple of word senses drifting toward the Hebrew (88:15, 88:34)."}
